# ===========================================================================
# Line-ending and binary handling rules for the whole repository.
#
# Policy:
#   * Text files are normalized to LF in the Git object store (text=auto)
#     and checked out with the platform native line ending by default.
#   * Windows-only scripts are checked out with CRLF; Unix shell scripts
#     are always LF so they remain executable on macOS/Linux.
#   * All binary assets, game data, compiled objects and third-party
#     binaries are explicitly marked binary so Git never converts,
#     merges or smudges them.
#
# Note: existing files were not mass-renormalized when this file was added
# (that would bury history in a single huge diff). Normalization happens
# naturally as files are touched. To normalize everything on purpose:
#     git add --renormalize .
# ===========================================================================

# --- Default: let Git auto-detect text --------------------------------------
* text=auto

# --- Explicit text line endings ---------------------------------------------
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.psm1      text eol=crlf

